  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "When expanding $(1+3x)^3(1+x)^7$, the coefficient of $x^2$ is $\\binom{7}{2}+\\binom{7}{1}\\binom{3}{1}3+\\binom{3}{2}3^2$. Explain where each term comes from.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\binom{7}{2}$ comes from $1\\times\\binom{7}{2}x^2$; $\\binom{7}{1}\\binom{3}{1}3$ comes from $\\binom{3}{1}3x\\times\\binom{7}{1}x$; $\\binom{3}{2}3^2$ comes from $\\binom{3}{2}(3x)^2\\times1$.\n\nMatch terms whose powers of $x$ add to 2.",
      "worked": "Match a term from the left expansion with a term from the right expansion so their powers of $x$ add to 2.\n\nThe constant term 1 on the left multiplies $\\binom{7}{2}x^2$ on the right, contributing $\\binom{7}{2}$.\n\nThe term $\\binom{3}{1}3x$ on the left multiplies $\\binom{7}{1}x$ on the right, contributing $\\binom{7}{1}\\binom{3}{1}3$.\n\nThe term $\\binom{3}{2}(3x)^2$ on the left multiplies the constant term 1 on the right, contributing $\\binom{3}{2}3^2$.\n\nThese are all possible pairings, so their coefficient contributions are added.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
